docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/SUMMARY.md-41-## Suggested WhatsApp message for Marcus
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/SUMMARY.md-42-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/SUMMARY.md:43:> oswa review done ✅ all 5 core pages reviewed against the briefs + fresh SERP data. honest verdict: the writing itself is genuinely good — right structure, right tone — but none are publishable yet. main issues: AHPRA/TGA compliance (unbalanced "safe"/"life-changing" claims, GLP-1/semaglutide mentions — TGA restricts naming prescription med classes in public advertising), Medicare/BMI wording that overpromises vs the actual MBS criteria, single dollar fees quoted where the briefs said not to, and leftover working notes (one CTA on the bypass page literally says gastric sleeve 😅). important context for the writer: a fair chunk of the flagged wording (the BMI framing, the "safe for most candidates" line, the GLP-1 coverage) came from OUR briefs — she followed them. so this is a fix pass on drafts + briefs together, and every issue has a paste-ready rewrite in the review docs. two things i need from you/client: (1) are surgeries at SJOG murdoch/subiaco (briefs) or mount private/the park/waikiki (all 5 drafts say this — she may have newer info)? (2) how does the practice want to handle mentioning GLP-1/medical weight management publicly — that's a TGA/legal call that affects every page. sending the review pack now.
--
