docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md:429:> No online checklist can decide suitability. For MBS items, a BMI below 35 does not meet the threshold, and BMI 35–39.9 without at least one major obesity-related condition also does not meet the threshold; a procedure may also be deferred if assessment identifies unacceptable surgical or anaesthetic risk, unresolved medical issues or difficulty completing required follow-up. Your surgeon makes an individual assessment.
