docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md-5-- Finding: Medicare item-number wording is not accurate enough for a Roux-en-Y page. Item 31572 is the Roux-en-Y gastric bypass item; 31581 is for biliopancreatic diversion with or without duodenal switch, so listing both as if they apply to this primary laparoscopic gastric bypass page is a compliance risk.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md:6:  Quote: "Medicare item numbers 31572 and 31581 attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md:7:  Suggested rewrite: "Medicare rebates may apply when MBS criteria are met. For Roux-en-Y gastric bypass, the relevant MBS item is 31572; your surgeon will confirm the appropriate Medicare item number, rebate eligibility and any private health fund requirements before surgery. Private health insurance with appropriate hospital cover may contribute to hospital and theatre costs, but out-of-pocket costs vary by fund and policy."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md-8-
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md:9:- Finding: The BMI eligibility sentence is broader than current MBS wording and could mislead readers about Medicare eligibility. MBS explanatory note TN.8.29 generally describes clinically severe obesity as BMI 40 or higher, or BMI 35 or higher with major medical comorbidities, with clinical judgment and population differences noted.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md-10-  Quote: "A gastric bypass is generally considered suitable for adults with a BMI of 35 or higher, or a BMI of 30–35 with associated weight-related health conditions such as type 2 diabetes, high blood pressure, sleep apnoea, or reflux."
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/_worklog/gastric-bypass-perth-codex.md-11-  Suggested rewrite: "Gastric bypass suitability is assessed individually. For Medicare-funded bariatric surgery, clinically severe obesity is generally described as a BMI of 40 or higher, or a BMI of 35 or higher with major medical comorbidities, although your surgeon will consider your full health picture and whether any population-specific or clinical factors apply. Some lower BMI ranges may be discussed for selected metabolic-surgery patients, but Medicare rebate eligibility must be confirmed by the surgical team."
